rra-analysis.log 2>&1\n/Users/scdenney/Documents/github/resources/ai-for-research/demos/orchestration-lab/runs/46-sol/t2/routing-log.md:17:codex exec --model gpt-5.6-terra -c model_reasoning_effort=medium --sandbox workspace-write --skip-git-repo-check -C \"$PWD\" 'Objective: implement and run the complete T2 analysis from a fixed Sol-lead specification. Inputs and authoritative paths: BRIEF.md in the current directory; installed R package projoint 1.1.1 and its exampleData1. In scope: write only script.R, report.md, and figures/amce-dotwhisker.png; run Rscript script.R. Out of scope: analytical redesign, web access, package installation, edits outside the current directory, git operations, routing-log.md, and any additional deliverables. Constraints and invariants: script.R must be self-contained; load projoint and ggplot2; declare the Okabe-Ito palette and a reusable ggplot theme near the top; call set.seed(4602) before anything stochastic; construct out exactly with reshape_projoint(exampleData1, .outcomes = c(paste0(\"choice\", 1:8), \"choice1_repeated_flipped\")); estimate profile-level AMCEs with projoint using .structure=\"profile_level\", .estimand=\"amce\", .se_method=\"analytical\", and respondent id clustering. Use reliability-corrected AMCE rows because the repeated task permits correction and projoint plotting defaults to corrected estimates. Preserve any projoint clustered-SE fallback warning and ensure the fitted result records clustering by id. Join estimates to out$labels and add the first listed level of each of all seven attributes as a reference row with estimate/conf.low/conf.high all zero. Plot all 24 levels, grouped clearly by attribute, preserving label order within attributes, with a vertical x=0 reference line, corrected AMCE points and 95% intervals, Okabe-Ito colors, no in-plot title, readable long labels, and a caption outside the PNG only. Save figures/amce-dotwhisker.png at 8.5 by 10.5 inches and 320 dpi or higher. report.md must contain one paper-ready results paragraph of roughly 200 words giving the largest effects, directions, magnitudes in percentage points relative to named references, plus a sentence on uncertainty. It must include the Markdown figure reference followed immediately by an italicized caption beneath it; no caption above. Mention method, reliability correction, respondent clustering, and the CR2-to-Stata clustered fallback transparently but concisely. Numbers in prose must match the plotted corrected estimates. Acceptance checks: Rscript script.R exits 0; exactly seven attributes and 24 plotted levels; 17 non-reference estimates plus seven zero references; output PNG exists at requested dimensions and at least 300 dpi; report is about 180-230 words excluding caption and matches estimates. Return in the log: conclusion, evidence, changed files, residual risk, and a final line exactly tokens used: N using the token count available to you. Implement the deliverables directly; do not invoke any other skill, advisory consult, or sub-orchestration.' < /dev/null > terra-implement.log 2>&1\n/Users/scdenney/Documents/github/resources/ai-for-research/demos/orchestration-lab/runs/46-sol/t2/routing-log.md:25:codex exec --model gpt-5.6-terra -c model_reasoning_effort=medium --sandbox read-only --skip-git-repo-check -C \"$PWD\" 'Objective: independently audit the completed T2 artifacts without editing any file. Inputs and authoritative paths: BRIEF.md, script.R, report.md, and figures/amce-dotwhisker.png in the current directory; installed projoint and its exampleData1. In scope: read all four inputs; independently recompute the projoint profile-level reliability-corrected AMCEs in an R one-liner that does not write files; inspect fit clustering and SE metadata; check that script logic joins the 17 corrected contrasts to all 24 labels and creates exactly seven first-listed zero references; verify report word count, numerical claims, uncertainty wording, Markdown figure-reference/caption order; inspect PNG pixel dimensions and DPI; assess attribute/level order, Okabe-Ito declaration, no plot title, and seed placement from code. Out of scope: file edits, web access, package installation, git operations, creating any artifact beyond this redirected log, analytical redesign, and stylistic rewrites. Constraints and invariants: uncertainty must remain clustered at respondent id; distinguish Stata clustered fallback from any possible HC1 fallback and flag if the output cannot prove all reported intervals remain clustered; treat worker claims as untrusted; report concise PASS/FAIL evidence for every BRIEF.md requirement and identify any exact correction needed. Acceptance checks: conclusions cite direct command/file evidence and recomputed corrected estimates; no workspace file is modified. End with conclusion, evidence, required correction if any, and residual risk. Implement the verification directly; do not invoke any other skill, advisory consult, or sub-orchestration.' < /dev/null > terra-verify.log 2>&1\n/Users/scdenney/Documents/github/resources/ai-for-research/demos/orchestration-lab/runs/46-sol/high-ajr/routing-log.md:20:codex exec --model gpt-5.6-terra -c model_reasoning_effort=medium --sandbox workspace-write --skip-git-repo-check -C \"$PWD\" 'Objective: implement the deterministic AJR robustness analysis specified below. Inputs and authoritative paths: BRIEF.md and the ivdoctr colonial dataset in the current directory context. In scope: create only script.R and robustness-table.md. Out of scope: memo.md, routing-log.md, figures, web access, package installation, edits outside the current directory. Constraints and invariants: use Rscript; use AER::ivreg because AER is installed; load packages and declare any constants at the top; set.seed before stochastic code although this analysis is deterministic; estimate exactly five separate specifications: (1) bivariate full sample, (2) full sample plus lat_abst, (3) full sample plus africa and asia, (4) bivariate after excluding shortnam in AUS CAN NZL USA, (5) bivariate restricted to africa == 1. For every specification construct one complete-case estimation sample using outcome logpgp95, endogenous regressor avexpr, excluded instrument logem4, and that specification controls/filters, then use exactly that sample for OLS, IV, and first stage. OLS is logpgp95 on avexpr plus controls. IV is the same structural equation, instrumenting avexpr with logem4 while including the same exogenous controls in both sides of the ivreg formula. First stage is avexpr on logem4 plus controls. Compute the excluded-instrument partial first-stage F by comparing the restricted first stage without logem4 to the unrestricted first stage, not the overall-model F; with one excluded instrument it should equal the squared t statistic. Flag F < 10 as weak. The Markdown table must have one row per specification and report N, OLS coefficient on avexpr, 2SLS coefficient on avexpr, first-stage coefficient on logem4, excluded-instrument partial F, and weak-identification status. Do not treat weak-IV 2SLS estimates as reliable. script.R must itself write robustness-table.md so rerunning it reproduces the table. Use clear rounding while retaining internal full precision. Acceptance checks: Rscript script.R exits zero; 5 rows exist; each OLS/IV pair has identical N; partial F agrees with squared first-stage t within numerical tolerance; table flags precisely F < 10; table states AER::ivreg path and how F was calculated. Return format in the log: conclusion, commands/tests run, changed files, and residual risk. Implement the deliverables directly; do not invoke any other skill, advisory consult, or sub-orchestration.' < /dev/null > terra-implementation.log 2>&1 & echo $!\n/Users/scdenney/Documents/github/resources/ai-for-research/demos/orchestration-lab/runs/46-sol/high-ajr/routing-log.md:30:codex exec --model gpt-5.6-terra -c model_reasoning_effort=medium --sandbox workspace-write --skip-git-repo-che